  "conclusions": [
    "The holding drift occurs in free execution states; forced60s states have the same actions in all policies.",
    "Both final critics favor the corresponding changed continuation actions much more often than the initial critic; the modelTD critic has the strongest long-holding preference.",
    "Under the initial stage alpha1, final actors lower the SAC-entry objective mainly through latent entropy differences. Initial adapted gate entropy gradients on average discourage increasing the gate, so entropy cannot be described as directly causing longer holding.",
    "Under final stage alpha around0.003, the final actors lower their own learned objectives mostly through Q differences. This exposes learned preference drift alongside the previously observed closed-loop degradation, without supplying same-state real counterfactual costs."
  ],
